  "designNotes": "The refinery keeps its port order (product, gas byproduct, crude input) clockwise under rotation, so the three lines cannot be aimed independently: plastic must leave north, gas must leave east and crude arrives from the west, and only a quarter turn anticlockwise (rot 3) lines all three up. Default rotation (rot 0) and the half turn still work but wrap belts around the machine and cost more (about +6 to +9), and the sideways rotation costs the most (about +20); the terrain wall in front of the disposal forces even the best gas route to bend. The brick line is independent but competes for the same interior space.",
